        "2.1)\n",
        "\n",
        "$$f(x) = x^2 - 4x + 4$$\n",
        "$$f^{'}(x) = 2x - 4 = 0 \\rightarrow x = 2$$\n",
        "$$f^{''}(x) = 2$$\n",
        "$$ 2 > 0 $$\n",
        "So x = 2 is a critical point and the minimum value is f(2) = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "2.2)\n",
        "\n",
        "$$f(x) = x^3 - 3x^2$$\n",
        "$$f^{'}(x) = 3x^2 - 6x = 0 \\rightarrow x(3x-6)$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Critical points at x = 0 and x = 2.\n",
        "$$f^{''}(x) = 6x - 6$$\n",
        "Plug in x = 0,2\n",
        "For x = 0: $$f^{''}(x) = -6$$\n",
        "$$-6 < 0$$\n",
        "So f(0) = 0 is a maximum.\n",
        "For x = 2: $$f^{''}(x) = 6$$\n",
        "$$6 > 0$$\n",
        "So f(2) = -4 is a minimum\n",
        "So f(x) has a local minimum at (2,-4) and a local maximum = (0,0)\n",
        "\n",
        "2.3)\n",
        "$$f(x,y) = x^2-y^2$$\n",
        "$$∇f(x,y) = (\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}, \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y})$$\n",
        "$$= (2x, -2y)$$\n",
        "$$∇f(x,y) = (0,0) → 2x = 0, -2y = 0 → x = 0, y = 0$$\n",
        "Compute Hessian matrix:\n",
        "$$[2, 0]$$\n",
        "$$[0, -2]$$\n",
        "Find det(H) = (2)(-2) = -4.\n",
        "Since -4 < 0, the critical point at (0,0) is a saddle point."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "t--NyqQ-kKwa"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3.)\n",
        "$$\\mathcal{L}(x, y, z, \\lambda) = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - λ(x+2y+z-6)$$\n",
        "$$\\frac{∂ \\mathcal{L}}{∂x} = 2x - \\lambda → 2x = \\lambda $$\n",
        "$$\\frac{∂ \\mathcal{L}}{∂y} = 2y -2\\lambda → 2y = 2\\lambda$$\n",
        "$$\\frac{∂ \\mathcal{L}}{∂z} = 2z - \\lambda → 2z = \\lambda$$\n",
        "$$\\frac{∂ \\mathcal{L}}{∂\\lambda} = x + 2y + z = 6$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Solve for critical points:\n",
        "$$x = \\frac{\\lambda}{2}, y = \\lambda , z = \\frac{\\lambda}{2}$$\n",
        "Sub into constraint equation:\n",
        "$$\\frac{\\lambda}{2} + 2\\lambda + \\frac{\\lambda}{2} = 6$$\n",
        "$$3\\lambda = 6$$\n",
        "$$\\lambda = 2$$\n",
        "Critical point at (1, 2, 1).\n",
        "$$f(1,2,1) = 1 + 4 + 1 = 6$$\n",
        "Choose another valid point (6,0,0):\n",
        "$$f(6,0,0) = 36 $$\n",
        "$$6 < 36$$\n",
        "So, the value of 6 at critical point (1,2,1) must be a minimum extrema.\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "The role of the constraint is to restrict the search space to points lying only of the line x + 2y + z = 6."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Or8pdmDwpatG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "4.)\n",
        "$$J(w1) = (w1-5)^4 + (w1-3)^2 +4$$\n",
        "$$\\frac{dJ}{dw1} = 4(w1-5)^3 + 2(w1-3)$$\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "$$w1^{(t+1)} = w1^{(t)} - η(\\frac{dJ}{dw1}|_{w1^{(t)}})$$\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "Iteration 1:\n",
        "$$w1^{(1)} = 2 - 0.1(-110) = 13$$\n",
        "Iteration 2:\n",
        "$$w1^{(2)} = 13 - 0.1(2068) = -193.8$$\n",
        "Iteration 3:\n",
        "$$w1^{(3)} = -193.8 - 0.1(-31427842.69) = 3142590.469$$\n",
        "Iteration 4:\n",
        "$$w1^{(4)} = -1.24\\times10^{19}$$\n",
        "Iteration 5:\n",
        "$$w1^{(5)} = 7.65\\times 10^{56}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The stochastic descent method on this cost function requires a much smaller learning rate, because at 0.1 the steps are far too big. The partial differentiation method would allow us to find the optima in just one step."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RMKbMZC_tZ9U"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "5.)\n",
        "$$L(w) = ||y-Xw||^2 + λ||w||^2$$\n",
        "Use property: $$||v||^2 = v^Tv$$ So\n",
        "$$L(w) = (y-Xw)^T(y-Xw)+λw^Tw$$\n",
        "$$=(y^T - w^TX^T)(y-Xw)+\\lambda w^Tw$$\n",
        "$$=y^Ty - y^TXw-w^TX^Ty + w^TX^TXw + \\lambda w^Tw$$\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "$$y^TXw = w^TX^Ty$$\n",
        "$$L(w) = y^Ty -2w^TX^Ty+w^TX^TXw +\\lambda w^Tw$$\n",
        "Take the gradient with respect to w:\n",
        "$$∇_wL(w) = -2X^Ty + 2X^TXw + 2\\lambda w$$\n",
        "Set to zero:\n",
        "$$-2X^Ty + 2X^TXw + 2\\lambda w = 0$$\n",
        "$$X^TXw + \\lambda Iw = X^Ty$$\n",
        "$$(X^TX + \\lambda I)w = X^Ty$$\n",
        "$$w = (X^TX+\\lambda I)^{-1}X^Ty$$\n",
        "Original Linear Regression: $$w = (X^TX)^{-1}X^Ty$$\n",
        "L2 Regularized: $$w = (X^TX+\\lambda I)^{-1}X^Ty$$\n",
        "This changes the solution by adding a positive constant λI. The impact of adding the L2 penalty is that adding $$\\lambda I$$\n",
        "ensures that $$(X^TX+\\lambda I)$$ is positive-definite and always invertible."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SlFyorxA9M2N"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "6.)\n",
        "Assumptions of Linear Regression\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "1. The relationship between the independent variable and the dependent variable is linear.\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "2. The error terms are independent of one another.\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "3. The variance of the residuals is constant across all values of x.\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "4. The error terms are normally distributed with a mean of zero.\n",
        "$$$$\n",
        "5. The datset does not contain extreme outliers."
      ],
